WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:06.190
I must kill Chloé this time.
I must not fail.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.110
Chloé d'Apchier is not the Beast.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.490
You've seen it with your own eyes.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.030
That doesn't matter.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.200
Lord Ruthven ordered me to put
an end to the trouble in Gévaudan.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.000
But he never told you to kill her.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.460
Do you realize how many lives
the Beast of Gévaudan has claimed?

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.250
I have no choice but to slay it.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.630
And Chloé is a curse-bearer.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.340
Bourreaus must execute
curse-bearers that have lost control.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.890
It's too late now. She's beyond help.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.480
That's why I must--

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.400
It's not too late!

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.990
Chloé d'Apchier can still be saved.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.990
And we're the ones who can do it.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.870
So I'm asking for your help, Jeanne.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.340
Chloé hasn't slain
a single denizen of Gévaudan.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.920
Not now or in the past.
That is the one thing I'm sure of.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.300
She was framed as the Beast.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.220
How is that possible? I thought...

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.890
You must ask her that yourself.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.980
But I'll ask you again the question
I posed at the mountain cabin.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.690
Will you slay Chloé d'Apchier?

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.070
Is that what you truly wish?

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:48.420
I mustn't wish for anything,
nor pray for anything, either.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.380
Why not?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.460
I don't know. But if I don't obey...

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.760
...someone else will again lose
their head in place of mine.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.260
Perhaps even you!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:10.850
I won't die! At least, not before you!

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:16.360
I promised I'd kill you
if you ever lost control.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.240
I love you.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.610
I can make your wish come true.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:23.030
It must be me.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.790
So out with it. What is it you truly wish?

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.540
Tell me, no matter how trivial a desire

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.630
or unlovely an emotion.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.090
Even if it's a curse.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.340
I'll do all in my power!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.930
H-Help.

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.680
Help.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.270
Please help!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:50.770
This has tormented me for so long.
I cannot stand much more.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.690
Please.

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.440
Help me.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.110
Help Chloé.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:00.200
Please help us, Vanitas!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.910
Leave it to me.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.210
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.260
Jean-Jacques!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.810
Are you all right?! Jean-Jacques!

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:55.730
Huh?!

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.190
This is your fault!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.480
No!

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.320
I don't wish to give up yet!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.780
You didn't want to give up?!
I spoke too soon because of you!

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.780
I'm not in the habit of
making doubtful promises!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.080
In fact, it's inconceivable!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.700
You're to blame!

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.410
What?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.380
Open your eyes, Jean-Jacques,
or whatever your name is!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.170
Please, Vanitas, he's been injured.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.800
Finally awake?

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:27.010
There's no time,
so I'll only say this once.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:30.390
Chloé d'Apchier's vengeance failed.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:36.850
I need <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>
if you want to save her!

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.190
Tell me where it is!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.480
I-I'm sorry, so sorry!

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.570
Please forgive me,
Master and Mistress Granatum!

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.610
Little Mistress...

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.990
Young Master...

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:57.040
Remember this well, Astolfo.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.460
Our ancestors risked their
lives battling vampire-kind,

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.170
thereby protecting
the people of this land.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:09.390
Should those fiends once again
bare their fangs against this world,

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:16.100
it is your duty as a member of
House Granatum to claim their heads.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:24.150
You need not learn to fight
if it is too much for you to bear.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:29.700
It is by no means cowardice
to be afraid to hurt someone,

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:32.490
for you have a kind soul.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.490
Yes, Mother.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:39.250
Astolfo, never forget
the kindness that you bear.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.920
Big brother.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.050
A vampire!

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.300
What should I do?!

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.220
I must summon an adult at once!

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.770
Marco!

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.810
Big brother, he's hurt!

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:07.610
Mother, Father, Emma...

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.700
I feel sorry for him.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.330
Wait here.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.420
Don't worry. I won't tell anyone.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:29.550
I'll bring a medicine
chest from our manor.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.850
Young Master?! Little Mistress?!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.480
It is time for your studies!

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:48.610
Sorry. I'm not very good at this.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:53.820
But I'm a vampire. Why are you doing this?

00:07:54.820 --> 00:08:00.540
I thought I should help people
whenever they're in need.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.620
Does it still hurt?

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.840
Shall I put a spell on it?!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.840
<i>Bisou Magique!</i>

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.970
Well, well? Does it still hurt? Does it?!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.520
No, it doesn't hurt anymore.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.400
Thank you!

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:32.030
So, what's your name?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.110
Astolfo.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.030
Oh.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:43.330
Thank you. You're a kind human, Astolfo.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.460
Young Master! Little Mistress!

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:56.550
They will be the death of me,
running off like this each day.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.730
Let me hear some more today, Astolfo.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:05.690
You mean about our house?

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.850
Yes.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.440
You're the first human
friend I've ever had.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.320
I'd like to know more about you.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.950
For instance, what your
family members are like,

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.280
and how you spend your days.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.660
I'm so interested in that!

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:25.870
Not all vampires are evil.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.830
We don't need swords.
We don't have to fight.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:33.260
We can get along fine
if we learn all about each other.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.560
Wh-Why did you...

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.020
Thank you.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:50.360
You're such a kindly human, Astolfo.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.520
And...

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:57.700
You're such a fool that it makes me laugh!

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:23.510
My mother, father, and sister
were slain by the Chasseurs' paladins.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.470
How does it feel?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:29.770
No one in your family will
ever say your name again.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:34.270
Astolfo. Poor little Astolfo.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:36.860
I'll say your name in their stead.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:44.660
After all, what are
friends for? Right, Astolfo?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.130
What was that?

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.220
Accursed vampires!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.110
Young Master!

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.570
Oh, dear! What happened here?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.950
I don't think we shall
get what we came for.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.210
So what now?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.870
Good question.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:32.880
Dante!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.460
Quack! You mind explaining what the hell--

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.880
Help me find my book!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:37.710
Huh?!

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:42.840
Behind you! Second floor, sixth shelf!
<i>The Book of Vanitas</i> is there!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.390
Find it, quick!

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.560
Otherwise, we'll all be trapped forever

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.100
in the closed world that
Chloé d'Apchier created!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.650
Very well! We'll help you for now!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.810
You sure about that?

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.690
It will all be in vain if we're
trapped here forever!

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:02.110
Do you really want to make Riche cry?!

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:07.200
And in any case, there's still
that matter concerning Vanitas.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:09.910
I'm afraid it will get ugly.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:16.040
Vanitas? What are you looking for?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:16.920
Got it!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.210
Hey, can you get this thing working?

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.090
What?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.130
If you know how, do it now!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.090
A-All right.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.760
What are you up to?

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:28.760
I will do exactly
what Chloé d'Apchier did.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.060
She is starting to merge with
the closed world she created.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:35.810
If we don't act quickly, there will
be no target for a reverse operation.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.440
I must stabilize her existence.

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:44.200
That's strange. This should activate it.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.700
Could it be broken?

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.830
Is the engine's core made of astermite?!

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:50.410
It is, but...

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.580
I believe it's a special kind.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:58.250
Chloé called it divine tearstone.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:04.970
Father, is the stone on this
book also made of astermite?

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:09.510
That's right, but it's
no ordinary astermite.

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:15.310
It's a special kind that's much
purer and far more powerful.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:20.360
It's known as blue tearstone
or divine tearstone.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.400
I'll help look for the book!

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.950
Vanitas?!

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.290
What happened to your hand?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:39.460
Never mind me. You must hurry!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:45.050
I must destroy...

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:54.430
...Chloé!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.990
Destroy!

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.530
Chloé.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:14.200
It's all right, Jean-Jacques.
I don't think Jeanne is out for blood.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:17.120
How did it come to this?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.790
She said she would finally
be free once this was all over.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:25.260
I thought she wouldn't
have to suffer any longer.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:30.140
Chloé d'Apchier, no doubt, intended
to die once her vengeance was done.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:30.970
What?

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.350
I know that face well.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.390
Chloé d'Apchier! Don't do this!

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.780
It's the self-satisfied,
self-absorbed look

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.110
of someone who has
selfishly decided to die alone.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.570
It makes me puke!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.410
That's absurd.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.450
Chloé... She wouldn't...

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.080
Jean-Jacques, let's try talking to Chloé!

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:01.460
We can get through to her!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:05.550
We may be so close to someone
and want to protect them so much,

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:09.510
but they'll never know
unless we tell them!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.260
Huh?

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.310
Astolfo!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:19.230
I will kill you.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:23.560
I will kill every last
one of you vampires!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:28.690
Commence

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.280
calculation.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:50.590
What?!

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:54.050
Even beheading them or chopping
them to pieces doesn't work.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:57.510
Just die already, you overgrown mutt!

00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:00.100
Well, Olivier? Answer me.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.980
Enough already, Roland.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:08.400
Even we won't be able to protect them
if this drags on much longer.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.280
If it comes to that,

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.070
do not hesitate.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.450
I know.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:18.950
Noé, Vanitas...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:40.140
He's faster and stronger than before!

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:45.770
That was even faster!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.070
Die!

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.530
All vampires!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:52.360
They must die.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.450
Begone from my sight!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.680
Astolfo.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:27.020
After all, what are friends for?
Right, Astolfo?

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:36.740
How dare you speak my name,
you accursed heretic!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.370
Young Master!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:42.620
You vampires never should have been born!

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.040
You are abominations that
should not be allowed to even exist!

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:51.750
That is why my brethren and
I must exterminate all vampires

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.380
and return this world
to its pristine state!

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:09.020
You wish to help this child?

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.310
Oh, I see.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:16.320
You, too, will need
a friend once this is all over.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.610
Now I see.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:24.910
You never once did speak of yourself
as having any sort of future.

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:31.460
Somewhere deep inside, I knew that,
but I was too afraid to ask.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:44.470
Why go through the trouble to build
weapons into those automated instruments?

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.270
After all, I will protect you.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:51.980
And why name them after
members of the d'Apchier family?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:58.650
They shall serve as
surrogates for these children.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:04.660
I will have my vengeance,
and they will have theirs, together.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.790
I understand now.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:14.250
She meant to die once all this was over.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.210
She blames herself for
the end of her family line.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:22.010
So she will have those automatons
kill her in an act of vengeance.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:26.180
Analysis complete. Coordinates set.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:29.270
Definitions changed. Alter phenomenon.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.400
Perpetuate existence!

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.110
Got it!

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.070
Hey, quack! I found it!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.120
Catch!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:59.670
Here in this closed world,
they all come to kill Chloé.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:01.630
Not only the dragoons,

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:05.010
but also the villagers,
the Chasseurs, and that bourreau.

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.180
They come back no matter
how many times I kill them.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:13.020
I have already slain them hundreds,
even thousands of times.

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:16.650
I wished to protect you, Chloé.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:20.440
But this is what <i>you</i> wished,

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.070
wasn't it?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:30.540
I must destroy this despicable
world before it's too late...

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.170
...and me along with it.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:39.000
I must set Jean-Jacques free now!

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:45.340
Chloé, you silly fool.
You don't have a clue.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:50.310
You don't know the first thing about me!

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:55.900
What's the use of being free without you?

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:07.160
I would plunge into the pits of hell
with you if you so wished.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:12.160
I'd go anywhere,
do anything if it was with you.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.580
Anything.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.090
But what's the point without you?!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:22.720
Don't think I could ever
be happy without you.

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:25.630
Don't go. Don't leave me.

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:28.100
Please.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:31.890
I'm begging you, Chloé.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:38.810
Don't leave me all alone!

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:05.010
"Just the Two of Us"

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
"Snow Flower"
